          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \,\colon\, D\to C
            is
            %em monadic
            iff it has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \,\colon\, C\to D
            such that – under the
            %a{:href => "monad#RelationBetweenAdjunctionsAndMonads"} relation between adjunctions and monads
            – the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\dashv U
            is that induced by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            which it induces – in which case it is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+adjunction"} monadic adjunction
          %p
            In this situation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is identified with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi EM
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} EM(U \circ F)
            of the monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi η
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %msub
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U \circ F, \eta, U\epsilon_F)
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functors"} forgetful functors
