                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is an equivalence (resp. isomorphism) of categories.
          %p
          #MonadicFunctor.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (monadic functor)
              %br/
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \colon D \to C
              is
              %em monadic
              (resp.
              = succeed ")" do
                %em strictly monadic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C\to D
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comparison+functor"} comparison functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{\mathbf{T}} \colon D \to C^{\mathbf{T}}
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
              (resp. an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              of
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+categories"} strict categories
              %br/
          %p
            In other words, up to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functors"} forgetful functors
            defined on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+categories"} Eilenberg-Moore categories
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+categories"} strict categories
          %ul
            %li
              If the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comparison+functor"} comparison functor
              is only
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful"} fully faithful
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/premonadic+functor"} premonadic
              or said to be
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+type"} descent type
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              is called
              %em monadic
              over a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              if there is any functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \colon D \to C
              which is monadic (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonadicFunctor"}
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#basic_properties Basic properties
          %p Every monadic functor is
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful
                (by the definition of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conservative"} conservative
                (by
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "monadicity+theorem#statement"} Beck’s monadicity theorem
          %p Moreover:
          %p
          #MonadicFunctorsCreateLimits.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functors"} monadic functors
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/created+limit"} create limits
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic functor
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/created+limit"} creates
                  all
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
                  that exist in its
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
              %li
                %p
                  creates all
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
                  that exist in its codomain and are preserved by the corresponding monad (or, equivalently, by the monadic functor itself).
            %p
          (e.g.
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#MacLane71"} MacLane 71, Exercise IV.2.2 (p. 138)
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Beware that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
              of monadic functors is
              %em not
              generally closed under
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            %p
              For a specific
              = succeed ":" do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counter-example"} counter-example
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+graphs"} reflexive graphs
              is monadic over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              via the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi RefGph
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RefGph \to Set
              sending a graph to its set of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edges"} edges
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+categories"} category of categories
              is monadic over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+graphs"} reflexive graphs
              via the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                      %mo →
                      %mi RefGph
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat \to RefGph
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
              is not monadic over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              (via any functor whatsoever, since monadic categories over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+categories"} regular categories
              which
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              is not).
            %p
              This is an instance of a general phenomenon: Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
              (e.g. any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              is of this form). Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjunction
              between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
              is monadic, and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjunction
              between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Set
                      %mrow
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ob
                        %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Set}^{\mathrm{Ob} A}
              is also monadic. But the composite adjunction between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Set
                      %mrow
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ob
                        %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Set}^{\mathrm{Ob} A}
              is often not monadic. For instance, if it is monadic, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              must be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barr-exact+category"} Barr-exact category
          %p
            However, it is possible to characterise when the composite of two functors is monadic. The following characterisation is Theorem 6.5 of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AM23b"} Arkor and McDermott 2025
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U : A \to B
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U' : B \to C
              be functors, and suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U'
              is monadic (and in particular has a left adjoint
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F'
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ′
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U' U
              is monadic if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+monad"} monadic relative to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F'
          %p
            Monadic functors have the following cancellation property:
          #Cancellation.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Consider a pair of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjunctions
              %svg{:height => "40.33pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 185.364 40.33", :width => "185.364pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
                %defs
